<task id="100" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Review read model and line decision endpoints</title>
    <phase>4 Review and approval (WP4) — wave W4-1</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>in-progress</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New authorized read and write routes over invoice lines; a missed check exposes another core record's invoice, a wrong write breaks I-1 totals or NFR-09 attribution.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Endpoint and service work on the existing Finance route and filter pattern; totals, lifecycle and Decision Record contracts come from 016, 014 and 074.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P4-A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>014, 016, 049</deps>
    <tags>bff, api, auth, write-path</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add the Invoice Review read model (header, totals, lines with status, findings with rule / version / clause, suggested adjustment, extraction page and box, Decision Record history) and the line decision routes (Accept; Reduce with approved amount and reason; Disallow with reason; one action on selected lines; Accept all Clean), recomputing totals through 016 and recording decisions through 074 — authorized on the invoice and only while it is In Review.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in ASP.NET Core Minimal APIs, ADR-008 endpoint filters, Dataverse conditional writes and read-model assembly.</role>

  <goal>InvoiceLineReviewEndpoints.cs with a read service and a line-decision service; correct 401 / 403 / disabled / 409 behaviour; decisions update line status, approved amount, reason, reviewer and totals per request and write the Decision Record(s) agreed in 074; the core-record access guard has a seeding proof.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-31 (reason mandatory for Reduce / Disallow), FR-07 and I-1 (client write of approved total refused), NFR-02 (3 s p90 at 150 lines), NFR-09, D-64 (bulk acceptance recorded as Accepted in bulk, never a label). Prototype: line decisions in the pane, one action on ticked rows with one reason, Accept all clean lines, Pending shown as Processing (README owner decisions, F-1). Columns: 010 (sprk_linestatus, sprk_approvedamount, sprk_adjustmentreason, sprk_reviewedby / on, sprk_extractionconfidence JSON with page and box), 012 (totals; statuscode numbers in its notes), 027 (sprk_invoicecorrection). Findings are sprk_signal rows on the invoice or line (026, 072 mapper). Routes: Api/Finance/FinanceEndpoints.cs:28-98 (group /api/finance, per-route AddFinanceAuthorizationFilter); Api/Filters/FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs (FromRoute :192, InvoiceEntitySet :234); policy keys server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/OperationAccessPolicy.cs:165-209 ("finance.read" = Read). Invoice access inherits from its core record via 013 stamping (ADR-034). Conditional writes: InvoiceReviewService.MarkDocumentConfirmedAsync (Services/Finance/InvoiceReviewService.cs:1171; MaxConditionalWriteAttempts :320). The /api/finance/invoice-review/* routes are the classification gate — do not extend them.</background>
    <relevant-files>
