    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="014" status="pending">Lifecycle service (In Review state)</dependency>
      <dependency task="016" status="pending">Totals calculator and persistence hook</dependency>
      <dependency task="049" status="pending">Invoices, lines, approval portion, Signals exist; 074's recorder and F-9 answer are upstream of it</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="074 ontology-r1 review K1/K3 (2026-10-17)">Recording billing Decision Records through BillingDecisionRecorder (074) brings two caller obligations.
- (1) Exactly-once. The writer is exactly-once only for retries made one after another; two concurrent calls with one decision id can both write, and a duplicate in an append-only ledger is permanent. So:
  - this task names its serialisation mechanism as an acceptance criterion. Examples: the job claims IIdempotencyService keyed by the decision id; an endpoint does a RowVersion-conditional status update and records only after it succeeds;
  - it adds a test for the concurrent same-id case.
- (2) Decider identity:
  - derive the deciding user from the authenticated principal, never from request input;
  - check invoice access through the UAC filter before recording;
  - pass no contact id. The recorder looks the contact up itself, as DecisionCommitService does; 074's fix round removes that parameter.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-90 / task 029 notes section 11 (2026-10-16)">Spaarke Core User and Basic User hold only Read on sprk_billingevent, and no AppendTo on sprk_billingcode / sprk_timekeeper. If any line-decision write runs as the caller (OBO), it would be refused: either write lines server-side through the owning service (the default, consistent with I-1 and the write-path rules), or raise the needed privileges (Write and Append on sprk_billingevent, AppendTo on sprk_billingcode and sprk_timekeeper) as an owner decision first. Do not widen roles inside this task without that decision.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-001, ADR-008, ADR-019">Own endpoints file; each route has its own AddFinanceAuthorizationFilter and RequireEbillingEnabled() (040, 503 ebilling.disabled); ProblemDetails with stable codes (e.g. ebilling.invoice.not_in_review, ebilling.line.reason_required).</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-31, root CLAUDE.md section 6">Reads: "finance.read" on sprk_invoices(route invoiceId). Writes: "ebilling.invoice.decide" (Write) on the same id. Every line id in a body must belong to that invoice (uniform 404 otherwise), checked before any write.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002, I-1">Only the server computes totals (016); no request field sets a total or a status. Writes only while statuscode is In Review (409 otherwise).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Reduce: approved amount at least 0 and less than billed, reason required. Disallow: reason required, approved 0. Accept: approved = billed. A Pending line cannot be decided (409). A multi-line request is all or nothing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-64">Accept all Clean and multi-line Accept write sprk_invoicecorrection rows (outcome Accepted in bulk, islabel false) per AI-sourced field of each affected line; single-line Accept writes none (101 owns the label outcomes).</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-30">Decision Records only through 074's recorder, at 074's F-9 granularity, idempotent by decision id.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-02">Read model built with a bounded number of Dataverse calls (none per line); record the count in notes.</constraint>
    <constraint source=".claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md">Placement BFF (B1 caller identity, B4 live request); publish-size delta; no new HIGH CVE; no package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="074 fix-round adversarial pass (2026-10-18), caller obligations of BillingDecisionRecorder">Callers that record billing decisions through BillingDecisionRecorder must:
- Derive the resolved Signal ids and the policy version id server-side, from the decision's own invoice and lines. Never take them from the request. The writer accepts any existing Signal or policy version (074 review K-2).
- Record before mutating, or run the recorder's reads first. Its refusals that depend on Dataverse reads (unknown policy version, missing Signal, undetermined subject, contact read fault) happen after Preflight, so a caller that changes invoice status first can be left with a changed status and no Decision Record (K-3).
- Serialise decisions per invoice (one at a time per invoice). The recorder's "already recorded" check and its create are not atomic (K-4).
- Build Values the same way on every attempt (same types, same decimal scale), so that an honest retry hashes to the same content (K-5, unless 074's follow-up normalises decimals).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ontology-r1 (2026-10-18), Signal evidence read rule (D-123)">SignalReadService strips text and source from every evidence line that is not a {table}:{guid} witness (fail-closed by design; ontology-r1 will not exempt billing lines). A merged billing Signal therefore reaches a reader with its 2nd and later reasons as bare codes marked withheld. The review page renders each reason's text from its reason code and the catalogue template, using the Signal's own invoice and line facts that the reader may see. It never relies on stored per-reason text. sprk_sentence (the primary sentence) stays readable. A withheld Duplicate reason renders only the withheld template. If stored per-reason text has to be readable as-is, send ontology-r1 a design that makes those lines access-checkable (a witness ref to the invoice or line) before building it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner D-128 / D-129 / D-130 (2026-10-19); ontology-r1 D-130 review">Line decisions drive spend:
- Counted spend sums the approved total (D-130 (2)). Today nothing recalculates sprk_approvedtotal after submission; IInvoiceTotalsService.RecalculateAsync's only caller is the 049 persister.
- So every line decision that changes an approved amount (Reduce, Disallow, Accept after a Reduce, bulk and accept-clean) calls RecalculateAsync in the same request, and a test shows sprk_approvedtotal changes.
- Credit lines: Disallow is allowed (D-128). Reduce is allowed to an amount between the billed credit and 0 (D-129 (3)). Never refuse a line for being negative.
- The matter and project stored rollup is refreshed by the rollup (FinanceRollupService), not here. Say in the notes when it runs after a decision.</constraint>
  </constraints>

