  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Read 074's notes (F-9 answer, recorder API), 016's calculator API, 010 / 012 option values, 049's notes (how findings and provenance are stored).</step>
    <step order="1">GET /api/finance/invoices/{invoiceId}/review: header (firm, firm invoice and tracking number, core record type / id / name, period, invoice date, status), totals, lines (type, date, timekeeper as billed and matched, hours, rate, amount, narrative, codes with confidence and as billed, status, approved amount, reason, reviewer), per-line and invoice-level findings (policy, version, clause quote and location, values read, severity, suggested adjustment, overridden marker), per-field page / box / confidence, Decision Record history, flags canRead / canDecide.</step>
    <step order="2">POST .../lines/{lineId}/decision; POST .../lines/decisions (selected lines, one action and reason, per-line amount for Reduce — the "apply suggestion to n lines" path); POST .../lines/accept-clean. Conditional line writes, totals through 016, Decision Records through 074.</step>
    <step order="3">Add the policy key; keep OperationAccessPolicyCompletenessTests green.</step>
    <step order="4">Tests: each outcome, reason and amount rules, Pending and not-In-Review refused, all-or-nothing, Accept all Clean touches only Clean lines, retry writes no second Decision Record, totals follow I-1; contract tests 401 / 403 / disabled / foreign line 404.</step>
    <step order="5">Seeding proof: caller without core-record access gets 403 on read and decide; remove the route filter, show the test fails, restore; record in notes.</step>
    <step order="6">dotnet build and dotnet test green; publish-size delta and vulnerable-package check recorded.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to "✅ [done]".</step>
    <step order="8">Record deviations (routes, DTO names, Dataverse call count) in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Per D-75 each line decision writes its own Decision Record (subject the line) through 074's recorder; if 074 has not landed that shape, STOP before the decision routes.</trigger>
    <trigger>If invoice access does not inherit from the core record in dev (013 stamping absent), STOP: the authorization would be wrong.</trigger>
    <trigger>Owner decided D-77: any internal user with Write access to the invoice may decide lines (not restricted to eligible approvers).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Spec section 11 row "Review / approval / export / rule endpoints" (overlap /api/finance/invoice-review/*); InvoiceReviewService.cs:248 only confirms a document as an invoice; grep finds no line read model or line decision code.</existing>
    <extension>Same Finance module and route group; a new endpoints file because nothing is shared with the classification gate. One policy key because no existing key names Write on an invoice.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The review page has no data and no line decision path, so FR-31 fails and I-2 can never be satisfied for approval (FR-35).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build, test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">Api/Finance/InvoiceLineReviewEndpoints.cs; Services/Finance/InvoiceReviewReadService.cs; Services/Finance/InvoiceLineDecisionService.cs</output>
    <output type="test">InvoiceLineDecisionServiceTests.cs; InvoiceReviewReadServiceTests.cs; InvoiceLineReviewEndpointsAuthorizationContractTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Every route returns 401 unauthenticated, 403 without access to the invoice's core record, 503 ebilling.disabled when the flag is off, and (writes) 409 when the invoice is not In Review.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Seeding proof recorded: removing the route filter makes the core-record access test fail.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Reduce without reason or with an amount outside 0 to billed is 400; Disallow without reason is 400; a Pending line is 409; a line of another invoice is 404 and nothing is written.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">After a decision the line carries status, approved amount, reason, reviewer and time, and invoice totals equal I-1 as computed by 016.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Accept all Clean changes only Clean lines and writes Accepted in bulk rows with islabel false; a multi-line request with one invalid line writes nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Decision Records follow 074's granularity; repeating a request with the same decision id writes no second record.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The read model returns findings with policy, version and clause, suggested adjustment, and per-field page and box; its Dataverse call count does not grow with line count.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build 0 errors; all tests green, including OperationAccessPolicyCompletenessTests.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size delta measured against a fresh master build and recorded in task notes; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Shared append points: FinanceModule.cs, EndpointMappingExtensions.cs (re-read before editing, add only this task's lines). In WP4 only 100 (W4-1) and 105 (W4-2) edit OperationAccessPolicy.cs; 101–104 reuse "ebilling.invoice.decide", 106 / 107 use "finance.read". No value-correction path here (101). Adjustment lines appear as lines of type Adjustment (102). Eligible approvers and canApprove come from 103's own route, so no P4-B task edits these files.</notes>

